            <ArticleTitle>The value of combined alpha- and beta-adrenoceptor blockade in angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The alpha- and beta-blocking effects of labetalol are such that during and following exercise the haemodynamic benefits of beta-blockade outweigh the unfavourable effects, because the latter are diminished by the concomitant minor degree of alpha-blockade.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
